# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment upload.
#
# ── Why this file exists ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Vercel's filesystem router turns every `.ts` file under `api/` into a public
# serverless function, and it makes no exception for tests. `api/payments/
# callback.test.ts` therefore deployed as the live route
# `/api/payments/callback.test`, and `api/callback/cpm/arp/collection.test.ts`
# as `/api/callback/cpm/arp/collection.test`. Both were confirmed reachable in
# production on 2026-08-25, answering:
#
#     GET /api/payments/callback.test              -> 500 FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED
#     GET /api/callback/cpm/arp/collection.test    -> 500 FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED
#     (log: "Vitest mocker was not initialized in this environment")
#
# Three separate problems, on the endpoints that take money:
#
#   • vitest and every test double were traced into the deployed bundle,
#     sitting alongside the real callback and settlement code;
#   • two public URLs answered 500 rather than 404, which is a working
#     signal to anything probing for live routes;
#   • the 500s were emitted from the payment namespace, so genuine callback
#     errors have to be picked out of noise that is not about payments at all.
#
# `api/_lib/*.test.ts` was never affected — Vercel already skips the
# underscore-prefixed directory — which is precisely why this went unnoticed:
# most of the suite lives there, and only the two endpoint-level test files
# ever became routes.
#
# Excluding the tests from the upload does not weaken them. They run in CI and
# locally through `npm test`, which reads the working tree, not the deployment.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
